\v 29 The temple servants: the sons¦109524 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Ziha.\f* Esav \add !(Esau)\add*, the sons¦109526 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Hasupha.\f* Hasufa, the sons¦109528 of Tabaeot, the sons¦109530 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Keros.\f* Keyros, the sons¦109532 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Siaha.\f* Siea, the sons¦109534 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Padon.\f* Padon, the sons¦109536 of Levana, the sons¦109538 of\f + \fr 5:29 \fqa Hagaba.\f* Hagava.
\v 30 the sons¦109540 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Akkub.\f* Akuv, the sons¦109542 of Uta, the sons¦109544 of Ketab, the sons¦109546 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Hagab.\f* Hagav, the sons¦109548 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Shamlai.\f* Shamlay, the sons¦109550 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Hanan.\f* Anan¦109551, the sons¦109552 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Giddel.\f* Gidel, the sons¦109554 of\f + \fr 5:30 \fqa Gahar\f* Gahar,
\v 31 the sons¦109556 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Reaiah.\f* Yair, the sons¦109558 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Rezin.\f* Retsin, the sons¦109560 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Nekoda.\f* Nekoda, the sons¦109562 of Chaseba, the sons¦109564 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Gazzam.\f* Gazam, the sons¦109566 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Uzza.\f* Ozias, the sons¦109568 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Paseah.\f* Paseah, the sons¦109570 of Asara¦109571, the sons¦109572 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Besai.\f* Besay, the sons¦109574 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Asnah.\f* Asnah, the sons¦109576 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Meunim.\f* Meunim, the sons¦109578 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Nephisim.\f* Nafish, the sons¦109580 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Bakbuk. \ft According to other readings, \fqa Acum, \ft or \fqa Acuph.\f* Bakbuk, the sons¦109582 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Hakupha.\f* Hakufa, the sons¦109584 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Harhur.\f* Harhur, the sons¦109586 of Pharakim, the sons¦109588 of\f + \fr 5:31 \fqa Bazluth.\f* Batslut,
\v 32 the sons¦109590 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Mehida.\f* Mehida, the sons¦109592 of Cutha, the sons¦109594 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Harsha\f* Harsha, the sons¦109596 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Barkos.\f* Barkos, the sons¦109598 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Sisera.\f* Sisera, the sons¦109600 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Temah\f* Temah, the sons¦109602 of\f + \fr 5:32 \fqa Neziah. \ft Another reading is, \fqa Nasith.\f* Netsiah, the sons¦109604 of Hatifa.
\p
\v 33 The sons¦109606 of Shelomoh's \add !(Solomon)\add* servants: the sons¦109609 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Hussophereth.\f* Soferet, the sons¦109611 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Peruda.\f* Perida, the sons¦109613 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Jaalah.\f* Ya'alah, the sons¦109615 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Darkon.\f* Darkon, the sons¦109617 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Giddel.\f* Isdael, the sons¦109619 of\f + \fr 5:33 \fqa Shephatia.\f* Shefatyah,
\v 34 the sons¦109621 of\f + \fr 5:34 \fqa Hattil.\f* Hatil, the sons¦109623 of\f + \fr 5:34 \fqa Pochereth-haz-zebaim, \ft Ezra 2:57.\f* Pokeret-Hatsvayim, the sons¦109625 of Sabie, the sons¦109627 of Sarothie, the sons¦109629 of\f + \fr 5:34 \ft Another reading is, \fqa Misaias.\f* Masias, the sons¦109631 of Gas¦109632, the sons¦109633 of Addus, the sons¦109635 of Subas, the sons¦109637 of Apherra, the sons¦109639 of Barodis¦109640, the sons¦109641 of Saphat, the sons¦109643 of Alon.
\p
\v 35 All¦109645 the¦109646 temple-servants and¦109648 the¦109649 sons¦109650 of Shelomoh's servants were three¦109654 hundred¦109654 and seventy two.
\v 36 These came up from¦109658\f + \fr 5:36 \fqa Telmelah.\f* Tel-Melah, and¦109660\f + \fr 5:36 \fqa Telharsha.\f* Tel-Harsha,\f + \fr 5:36 \fqa Cherub. Addan.\f* Charaathalan leading them, and¦109665 Allar;
\v 37 and¦109667 they couldn't¦109669 show their families¦109672, nor their stock, how¦109676 they were of¦109678 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*: the¦109678 sons¦109681 of¦109683\f + \fr 5:37 \fqa Delaiah. \ft Another reading is, \fqa Asan.\f* Delayah the¦109683 son¦109684 of¦109685\f + \fr 5:37 \fqa Tobiah \ft Another reading is, \fqa Baenan.\f* Ban, the¦109685 sons¦109687 of\f + \fr 5:37 \fqa Nekoda.\f* Nekoda, six¦109689 hundred¦109689 and fifty two.
\p
\v 38 Of the¦109694 priests¦109695, those who usurped the office of the priesthood¦109698 and¦109699 weren't found¦109701: the sons of\f + \fr 5:38 \fqa Habaiah, \ft or \fqa Hobaiah.\f* Havayah, the sons of¦109708\f + \fr 5:38 \fqa Hakkoz.\f* Hakots, the¦109708 sons of Jaddus, who married Augia one of the daughters¦109713 of\f + \fr 5:38 \fqa Barzillai. \ft Another reading is, \fqa Phaezeldaeus.\f* Barzilay, and¦109715 was called¦109716 after his name¦109719.
\v 39 When¦109721 the description of the kindred of these men was sought in¦109727 the¦109728 register and¦109730 wasn't¦109731 found, they were removed from executing the office of¦109734 the¦109734 priesthood¦109735;
\v 40 for Nehemyah \add !(Nehemiah)\add* and Attharias¦109741 told¦109737 them that they shouldn't¦109742 be partakers of the¦109744 holy¦109745 things until¦109746 a high priest wearing\f + \fr 5:40 \ft Grk. \fqa the manifestation and truth.\f* Urim and Tumim should arise¦109747.
\p
\v 41 So¦109756 all¦109757 those of Yisrael, from¦109760 twelve years old and¦109762 upward, beside male servants and¦109766 women servants, were in number forty two¦109770 thousand¦109770 and three¦109771 hundred¦109771 and sixty¦109772.
\v 42 Their male servants and¦109775 handmaids were seven¦109777 thousand¦109777 and three¦109778 hundred¦109778 and thirty and seven; the minstrels and singers, two¦109783 hundred¦109783 and forty five;
\v 43 four¦109786 hundred¦109786 and thirty and five camels, seven¦109790 thousand¦109790 and thirty six horses, two¦109793 hundred¦109793 and forty¦109794 five mules, and five thousand and five hundred¦109798 and twenty five animals of burden.
\p
\v 44 And¦109800 some of the¦109802 chief men of their families¦109806, when they came to God's¦109815 temple¦109813 that's¦109816 in¦109817 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, vowed to¦109820 set up the¦109821 house¦109822 again in its own place¦109826 according¦109828 to¦109828 their ability¦109831,
\v 45 and¦109832 to¦109833 give¦109833 into the¦109835 holy treasury¦109837 of the¦109838 works¦109839 one thousand minas\f + \fr 5:45 \ft A mina is about 570 grams or 1.25 pounds.\f* of gold¦109840, five thousand¦109842 minas¦109845 of silver, and¦109847 one hundred¦109850 priestly vestments.
\p
\v 46 The¦109853 priests¦109854 and¦109855 the¦109856 Levites and¦109858 some of¦109861 the¦109861 people¦109862 lived in¦109864 Yerushalem and¦109866 the¦109867 country¦109868. The¦109869 holy singers also¦109870 and¦109872 the¦109873 gatekeepers and¦109875 all¦109876 Yisrael lived in¦109878 their villages.
\s1 Worship resumes at the rebuilt altar
\p
\v 47 But¦109883 when the¦109884 seventh month was at hand, and¦109887 when the¦109889 children¦109890 of Yisrael were each¦109892 in¦109893 their own¦109895 place, they all came together with one purpose into¦109896 the¦109899 broad place before the¦109901 first¦109902 porch which is towards¦109898 the¦109906 east¦109907.
\v 48 Then¦109908 Yeshua the¦109911 son of¦109912 Yotsadak, his kindred the priests¦109919, Zorobabel¦109921 the¦109922 son of¦109923 Salathiail, and his kindred stood up and made¦109929 the¦109930 altar¦109931 of¦109932 the¦109932 god¦109933 of Yisrael ready¦109929
\v 49 to¦109935 offer burnt sacrifices on¦109936 it¦109937, in accordance with the¦109940 express commands in¦109941 the¦109942 book¦109944 of¦109945 Mosheh \add !(Moses)\add* the¦109945 man¦109946 of¦109947 God¦109948.
\v 50 Some people joined them out¦109953 of the¦109954 other nations¦109956 of the¦109957 land¦109958, and¦109959 they erected the¦109961 altar¦109962 onto its own place¦109965, because¦109967 all¦109975 the¦109976 nations¦109977 of the¦109978 land were hostile to¦109979 them and oppressed them; and they offered sacrifices¦109984 at the¦109986 proper times¦109987 and¦109988 burnt¦109989 offerings¦109989 to the¦109991 master both morning¦109992 and¦109993 evening.
\v 51 They also¦109996 held the feast of tabernacles, as it's commanded in¦110004 the¦110005 law¦110006, and¦110007 offered sacrifices¦110008 daily, as appropriate.
\v 52 After¦110015 that¦110016, they offered¦110017 the continual oblations and¦110019 the sacrifices¦110020 of the Sabbaths¦110021, of the new moons, and of all¦110026 the consecrated feasts.
\v 53 All those who'd made any vow¦110031 to God¦110033 began to¦110041 offer sacrifices¦110042 to God from¦110034 the¦110035 new¦110036 moon¦110036 of¦110037 the¦110037 seventh¦110038 month, although God's¦110049 temple¦110047 wasn't¦110050 yet¦110050 built¦110051.
\v 54 They gave¦110053 money¦110054, food, and¦110052 drink to¦110053 the¦110055 masons and carpenters.
\v 55 They also gave carts to the¦110065 people of Tsidon \add !(Sidon)\add* and¦110067 Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add*, that¦110070 they should bring cedar trees from¦110073 Levanon, and convey them in rafts to the harbour¦110083 of Yafo \add !(Joppa)\add*, according¦110084 to¦110084 the commandment which was written for them by Koresh \add !(Cyrus)\add* king¦110094 of¦110092 the¦110092 Persians.
\s1 The temple foundations are laid
\p
\v 56 In the¦110096 second¦110097 year¦110098 after his coming to¦110099 God's¦110104 temple¦110102 at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*, in the¦110103 second¦110108 month, Zorobabel¦110110 the¦110111 son of¦110112 Salathiail, Yeshua \add !(Jesus)\add* the son of¦110117 Yotsadak, their kindred, the Levitical priests¦110125, and¦110128 all¦110129 those who'd¦110130 come to Yerushalem out¦110132 of the¦110133 captivity began work.
\v 57 They laid the¦110139 foundation of¦110141 God's¦110142 temple¦110140 on the¦110143 new¦110144 moon¦110144 of¦110145 the second month, in¦110151 the¦110152 second year after they'd come¦110153 to Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* and¦110157 Yerushalem.
\v 58 They appointed the¦110161 Levites who¦110166 were at least twenty years old over the¦110168 master's works. Then Yeshua, with his sons¦110175 and¦110176 kindred, Kadmiel his brother¦110178, the¦110181 sons of Yeshua, Emadabun, and¦110183 the¦110184 sons¦110185 of Yoda¦110190 the¦110188 son¦110189 of¦110191 Henadad, and their sons¦110195 and kindred, all¦110198 the¦110191 Levites, with¦110193 one accord stood up and¦110196 started the¦110199 business, labouring to¦110203 advance the¦110205 works¦110206 in¦110207 God's house¦110209. So¦110212 the¦110214 builders built the¦110216 master's temple¦110217.\x + \xo 5:58: \xt Ezr 3:8-9.\x*
\p
\v 59 The priests¦110223 stood arrayed in their vestments with¦110225 musical instruments and¦110227 trumpets, and¦110229 the Levites the sons¦110232 of Asaf¦110233 with their cymbals,
\v 60 singing songs of thanksgiving and¦110240 praising¦110241 the master, according¦110242 to¦110242 the directions of King¦110244 David of¦110245 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*.
\v 61 They sang aloud, praising¦110251 the¦110252 master in songs of thanksgiving, because¦110249 his goodness and¦110258 his glory¦110260 are forever in¦110264 all¦110265 Yisrael.
\v 62 All¦110268 the¦110269 people¦110270 sounded trumpets and¦110272 shouted with a loud voice¦110274, singing songs of thanksgiving to¦110279 the master for the raising up of¦110282 the¦110282 master's house¦110283.
\v 63 Some of the¦110288 Levitical priests¦110289 and¦110292 of the heads of their families¦110297, the¦110299 elderly who'd¦110301 seen¦110302 the¦110303 former house¦110306 came to¦110307 the¦110308 building¦110310 of this one with¦110311 lamentation and¦110313 great¦110315 weeping.\x + \xo 5:63: \xt Ezr 3:12-13.\x*
\v 64 But¦110316 many with trumpets and¦110320 joy¦110321 shouted with a loud voice¦110324,
\v 65 so¦110325 that the¦110326 people¦110327 couldn't hear¦110329 the¦110330 trumpets for¦110332 the¦110333 weeping of¦110335 the¦110335 people¦110336, for¦110338 the¦110341 multitude sounded loudly, so¦110344 that it was heard far away.
\s1 Opposition to rebuilding the temple
\p
\v 66 Therefore when¦110347 the¦110349 enemies¦110350 of the¦110351 tribe¦110352 of Yehudah \add !(Judah)\add* and¦110354 Benyamin heard¦110348 it, they came¦110357 to¦110357 know¦110357 what that noise¦110360 of trumpets meant.\x + \xo 5:66: \xt Ezr 4:1.\x*
\v 67 They learnt that¦110365 those who returned¦110364 from¦110367 captivity built the¦110371 temple¦110372 for the master, the god¦110375 of Yisrael.
\v 68 So¦110377 they went¦110378 to¦110378 Zorobabel¦110380 and¦110381 Yeshua, and¦110383 to the chief men of the families, and said to¦110388 them, “We'll build together with you¦110391.
\v 69 Because¦110393 we, just like you, obey your master, and¦110399 sacrifice to¦110395 him from¦110402 the days¦110403 of King¦110405 Esar-Hadon\f + \fr 5:69 \ft Another reading is, \fqa Asbacaphath.\f* of the Assyrians, who brought us here¦110410.”
\p
\v 70 Then¦110411 Zorobabel¦110414, Yeshua \add !(Jesus)\add* and the chief men of the families of Yisrael said¦110412 to them, “It¦110413 isn't for you¦110427 to¦110429 build¦110429 the¦110430 house¦110431 for the master our god¦110433.
\v 71 We¦110435 ourselves alone¦110437 will build for the¦110439 master of¦110441 Yisrael, as King¦110449 Koresh \add !(Cyrus)\add* of the Persians has commanded us.”
\v 72 But¦110452 the¦110454 heathen of the¦110457 land¦110455 pressed hard on¦110458 the¦110459 inhabitants of Yehudah, cut off their supplies, and hindered their building¦110465.
\v 73 By their secret plots¦110467, and¦110466 popular persuasions and¦110469 commotions, they hindered the finishing of the¦110475 building¦110476 all¦110477 the¦110478 time¦110479 that¦110480 King¦110483 Koresh lived¦110481. So¦110485 they were hindered from building¦110488 for two¦110490 years¦110489, until¦110491 Dareyavesh's reign.
\c 6
\s1 The rebuilding resumes
\p
\v 1 Now in¦110495 the¦110497 second¦110498 year¦110499 of Dareyavesh's \add !(Darius)\add* reign, Hagay and¦110505 Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add* the¦110507 son of¦110508\f + \fr 6:1 \fqa Iddo. \ft Another reading is, \fqa Eddin\f* Ido, the prophets¦110511, prophesied¦110503 to¦110512 the Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* in¦110517 Yehudah and¦110520 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* in the¦110523 name¦110524 of the master, the god¦110526 of Yisrael.\x + \xo 6:1: \xt Ezr 4:24; 5:1.\x*
\v 2 Then¦110530 Zorobabel¦110532 the¦110533 son of¦110534 Salathiail and¦110536 Yeshua the¦110538 son of¦110539 Yotsadak stood¦110531 up and began to¦110542 build¦110542 the¦110543 master's house¦110544 at Yerushalem, the¦110553 master's prophets¦110552 being with them and helping them.
\p
\v 3 At the same time Tatenay\f + \fr 6:3 \fqa Tattenai.\f* the governor of Aram \add !(Syria)\add* and Foinikai came to them, with Shetar-Bozenay\f + \fr 6:3 \fqa Shetharbozenai\f* and his companions, and said to them,\x + \xo 6:3: \xt Ezr 5:3.\x*
\v 4 “By whose authority do you build this house and this roof, and perform all the other things? Who are the builders who do these things?”
\v 5 Nevertheless, the¦110607 elders¦110613 of¦110610 the¦110610 Yehudim obtained favour, because¦110603 the¦110612 master had visited the¦110614 captives¦110608;
\v 6 and¦110616 they weren't hindered from building¦110620 until¦110621 such time as communication was made to Dareyavesh about¦110625 them, and¦110627 his answer received.
\s1 The officials ask Dareyavesh to investigate
\p
\v 7 A copy of the letter which Tatenay, governor of Aram and Foinikai, and Shetar-Bozenay, with their companions, the rulers in Aram and Foinikai, wrote and sent to Dareyavesh:
\p
\v 8 “To King Dareyavesh, greetings. Let it be fully known to our lord the king, that having come into the country of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*, and entered into the city of Yerushalem, we found in the city of Yerushalem the elders of the Yehudim that were of the captivity
\v 9 building a great new house for the master of hewn and costly stones, with timber laid in the walls.
\v 10 Those works¦110704 are being done with great speed. The¦110711 work¦110712 goes on prosperously in their hands¦110715, and it's¦110716 being accomplished with all¦110719 glory¦110720 and¦110721 diligence¦110707.
\v 11 Then¦110724 asked we these elders¦110727, saying, ‘By whose authority are you¦110731 building¦110733 this¦110734 house¦110735 and¦110737 laying the¦110738 foundations of these works¦110739?’
\v 12 Therefore¦110743, to the¦110746 intent that we might give knowledge to¦110747 you¦110748 by writing¦110750 who¦110752 were the¦110754 leaders, we questioned them, and¦110756 we required of them the names in writing of their principal men.
\v 13 So they gave us this¦110763 answer¦110765, ‘We're¦110768 the¦110770 servants of¦110772 the¦110772 master who¦110774 made heaven¦110775 and¦110776 earth¦110778.
\v 14 As for this house¦110781, it was built¦110780 many years¦110783 ago by a great¦110789 and¦110790 strong¦110791 king¦110786 of¦110787 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, and¦110792 was finished.
\v 15 But when our fathers¦110797 sinned¦110800 against the¦110802 master of¦110804 Yisrael who's¦110806 in heaven, and provoked him to¦110808 anger, he¦110809 gave them over into the hands¦110811 of King¦110813 Nevukadnetsar \add !(Nebuchadnezzar)\add* of Bavel, king¦110815 of the¦110816 Kasdim \add !(Chaldeans)\add*.
\v 16 They pulled down¦110821 the¦110818 house¦110820, burnt it, and¦110823 carried away the¦110824 people¦110825 captive to Bavel.
\v 17 But¦110830 in¦110829 the¦110831 first¦110832 year¦110833 that Koresh \add !(Cyrus)\add* reigned over the country¦110836 of Bavel, King¦110840 Koresh wrote¦110838 that¦110839 this¦110842 house¦110843 should be rebuilt.
\v 18 The¦110847 holy vessels¦110849 of gold¦110851 and¦110852 of silver¦110854 that¦110855 Nevukadnetsar had carried¦110856 away out of¦110859 the¦110859 house¦110860 at Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* and¦110864 had set up in¦110867 his own temple¦110870, those King¦110876 Koresh brought out¦110877 of¦110878 the¦110878 temple¦110879 in¦110881 Bavel, and¦110883 they were delivered¦110884 to¦110884 Zorobabel¦110886 and to Sheshebatsar\f + \fr 6:18 \ft Another reading is, \fqa Sabunassarus.\f* the¦110887 governor,
\v 19 with commandment that he¦110891 should carry¦110893 away all¦110894 these vessels¦110896, and put them in¦110899 the¦110900 temple¦110901 at Yerushalem, and¦110905 that the¦110906 master's temple¦110907 should be built on¦110911 its site.
\v 20 Then¦110914 Sheshebatsar, having come¦110917 here, laid the¦110919 foundations¦110920 of¦110921 the¦110921 master's house¦110922 which is in¦110925 Yerushalem. From¦110928 that¦110929 time to¦110935 this we're still building. It isn't yet fully completed.’
\v 21 Now¦110937 therefore¦110938, if¦110939 it seems good, Oh king¦110941, let a search be made among the¦110944 royal archives of¦110947 our lord the¦110947 king that are in¦110943 Bavel.
\v 22 If¦110950 it's¦110958 found that the¦110959 building¦110960 of¦110961 the¦110964 master's house¦110962 which is in¦110965 Yerushalem has been done with the consent of King Koresh, and it seems good to our lord the king¦110971, let him send us directions about¦110975 these things.”
\s1 Dareyavesh orders support for the rebuilding
\p
\v 23 Then¦110977 King¦110979 Dareyavesh \add !(Darius)\add* commanded that a search be made among¦110983 the¦110984 archives that were laid up at Bavel \add !(Babylon)\add*. So¦110990 at Ahmeta the palace, which is in the country¦110999 of Maday \add !(Media)\add*, a scroll was found¦110991 where these things were recorded:\x + \xo 6:23: \xt Ezr 6:1.\x*
\v 24 “In the first year of Koresh's reign, King Koresh commanded to build up the master's house which is in Yerushalem, where they sacrifice with continual fire.
\v 25 Its height will be sixty cubits, and the breadth sixty cubits, with three rows of hewn stones, and one row of new wood from that country. Its expenses are to be given out of King Koresh's house.
\v 26 The¦111056 holy vessels¦111058 of¦111059 the¦111062 master's house¦111060, both¦111063 gold¦111064 and¦111065 silver¦111066, that¦111090 Nevukadnetsar took¦111068 out of¦111071 the¦111071 house¦111072 at Yerushalem and¦111076 carried¦111077 away to¦111088 Bavel, should be¦111088 restored to¦111089 the house at Yerushalem, and be set in the place¦111091 where they were before.”
\v 27 Also¦111094 he commanded that Tatenay the governor of Aram \add !(Syria)\add* and¦111099 Foinikai, and¦111101 Shetar-Bozenay, and¦111103 their companions, and¦111106 those who¦111107 were appointed rulers¦111113 in¦111109 Aram and¦111111 Foinikai, should be careful not to¦111114 meddle with the¦111115 place¦111116, but¦111118 allow Zorobabel¦111122, the master's servant, and governor of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add*, and the¦111128 elders¦111129 of¦111134 the¦111134 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, to¦111137 build¦111137 that house¦111133 of¦111139 the¦111139 master in its place¦111140.
\v 28 “I¦111142 also¦111143 command to¦111146 have it built¦111146 up whole again; and¦111147 that they look diligently to help those who are of the captivity of Yehudah, until¦111157 the¦111162 master's house¦111161 is finished,
\v 29 and¦111164 that out of the¦111166 tribute of Coele-Syria and¦111170 Foinikai a portion will be carefully¦111172 given to these men for the¦111176 sacrifices¦111179 of the¦111180 master, that is, to Zorobabel¦111182 the governor for bulls¦111185, rams, and lambs¦111189,
\v 30 and also corn, salt¦111195, wine¦111197 and¦111198 oil¦111199, and that continually¦111200 every year¦111202 without further question, according as¦111203 the¦111205 priests¦111206 who¦111207 are in¦111208 Yerushalem may direct to¦111212 be daily spent,
\v 31 that¦111215 drink offerings may be made to the¦111218 Most High God¦111219 for¦111222 the¦111223 king¦111224 and¦111225 for his children¦111227, and¦111228 that¦111231 they may pray for their lives¦111233.”
\v 32 He commanded that¦111236 whoever should transgress, yes, or neglect anything written¦111242 here, a beam will be taken out¦111247 of his own¦111249 house, and¦111251 he'll be hanged on¦111252 it¦111253, and¦111255 all his goods seized for the¦111256 king.
\v 33 “Therefore may the master, whose name¦111268 is called¦111270 on¦111270 there¦111271, utterly destroy every¦111273 king¦111274 and¦111275 nation¦111276 that stretches out his hand¦111280 to¦111282 hinder or¦111283 damage¦111284 that¦111285 house¦111286 of the¦111289 master in¦111290 Yerushalem.
\v 34 I¦111292, King¦111293 Dareyavesh have ordained that¦111298 these things be¦111299 done with diligence.”
\c 7
\s1 The completed temple is dedicated
\p
\v 1 Then¦111300 Tatenay the governor¦111302 of¦111315 Coele-Syria and Foinikai, and Shetar-Bozenay, with their companions, following King¦111316 Dareyavesh's \add !(Darius)\add* commandments,\x + \xo 7:1: \xt Ezr 6:13.\x*
\v 2 very carefully supervised the¦111320 holy work, assisting the¦111325 elders¦111326 of the¦111327 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add* and¦111329 rulers of the temple.
\v 3 So¦111331 the¦111334 holy work¦111336 prospered, while Hagay and¦111339 Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add* the¦111341 prophets¦111342 prophesied.
\v 4 They finished these things by the commandment of the master, the god of Yisrael, and with the consent of Koresh \add !(Cyrus)\add*, Dareyavesh, and Artahshashta \add !(Artaxerxes)\add*, kings of the Persians.
\v 5 So the holy house was finished by the twenty-third day of the month Adar, in the sixth year of King Dareyavesh.
\v 6 The¦111381 children¦111382 of Yisrael, the¦111385 priests¦111386, the¦111388 Levites, and¦111390 the¦111391 others who¦111393 returned from¦111394 captivity who joined them did what was written in¦111401 the¦111402 book¦111404 of Mosheh \add !(Moses)\add*.
\v 7 Because the¦111408 dedication of¦111410 the¦111410 master's temple¦111411, they offered one hundred¦111415 bulls¦111414, two¦111417 hundred rams, four hundred lambs¦111418,
\v 8 and twelve male goats for¦111421 the sin¦111422 of all¦111423 Yisrael, according to¦111427 the number¦111428 of the twelve princes of the tribes of Yisrael.
\v 9 The¦111437 priests¦111438 and¦111439 the¦111440 Levites stood¦111436 arrayed in their vestments, according¦111442 to¦111442 their kindred, for the services of the master, the god¦111449 of Yisrael, according to the¦111452 book¦111454 of Mosheh. The¦111456 gatekeepers were at every gate¦111460.
\s1 The returned exiles celebrate the Passover
\p
\v 10 The¦111463 children¦111464 of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* who¦111466 came out¦111467 of captivity held the¦111470 Passover¦111471 the¦111473 fourteenth¦111474 day of¦111475 the¦111475 first¦111476 month, when¦111478 the¦111480 priests¦111481 and¦111482 the¦111483 Levites were sanctified together,
\v 11 with all¦111487 those who returned from captivity; for they were sanctified. Because the¦111495 Levites were all sanctified together,
\v 12 and¦111500 they offered the¦111502 Passover¦111503 for all¦111504 who returned from captivity, for their kindred the priests¦111514, and¦111515 for themselves.
\v 13 The¦111519 children¦111520 of Yisrael who¦111522 came out¦111523 of the¦111524 captivity ate, even all¦111526 those who'd¦111527 separated themselves from¦111529 the¦111530 abominations¦111531 of the¦111532 heathen of the¦111534 land¦111535, and sought¦111536 the¦111537 master.
\v 14 They kept the feast of unleavened¦111544 bread seven¦111545 days¦111546, rejoicing before¦111548 the master,
\v 15 because¦111550 he'd turned the¦111552 counsel of¦111554 the¦111554 king¦111555 of Ashur \add !(Assyria)\add* towards them, to¦111557 strengthen their hands¦111561 in the¦111564 works¦111565 of the master, the god¦111567 of Yisrael.
\c 8
\s1 Ezra comes to Yerushalem
\p
\v 1 After these things, when¦111569 Artahshashta \add !(Artaxerxes)\add* the¦111575 king¦111577 of the Persians reigned, Ezra came, who was the son of Azaryah, the son of Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add*, the son of Hilkiyah, the son of Shalem,\x + \xo 8:1: \xt Ezr 7:1.\x*
\v 2 the son of Tsadok, the son of Ahituv, the son of Amaryah, the son of Ozias,\f + \fr 8:2 \ft The Vatican MS. omits \fq the son of Memeroth, the son of Zaraias, the son of Savias.\f* the son of Merayot, the son of Zerahyah, the son of Zerahyah, the son of Buki, the son of Avishua, the son of Pinhas, the son of Eleazar¦111602, the son of Aharon \add !(Aaron)\add*, the chief priest.
\v 3 This¦111609 Ezra went up from¦111612 Bavel \add !(Babylon)\add* as a skilled scribe¦111615 in¦111618 Mosheh's \add !(Moses)\add* law¦111621, which¦111614 was¦111617 given by¦111624 the¦111625 god¦111626 of¦111627 Yisrael.
\v 4 The¦111632 king¦111633 honoured him, for¦111636 he¦111638 found favour in his sight in all¦111640 his requests.
\v 5 There went up with him also some of the children of Yisrael, and of the priests, Levites, holy singers, gatekeepers, and temple servants to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*
\v 6 in the seventh year of Artahshashta's reign, in the fifth month (this was the king's seventh year); for they left Bavel on the new moon of the first month and came to Yerushalem, by the prosperous journey which the master gave them\f + \fr 8:6 \ft Some MSS. omit \fq for his sake.\f* for his sake.
\v 7 Because¦111699 Ezra had very¦111701 great skill, so that¦111705 he omitted nothing¦111706 of¦111710 the¦111710 law¦111711 and¦111713 commandments¦111716 of the¦111715 master, but taught¦111717 all¦111718 Yisrael the¦111719 ordinances and¦111722 judgements¦111723.
\s1 The king's letter authorising Ezra's work
\p
\v 8 Now the¦111726 commission, which¦111741 was written from¦111729 King¦111731 Artahshashta, came to¦111732 Ezra the¦111734 priest¦111735 and¦111736 reader of¦111738 the¦111744 master's law¦111739, was¦111742 as follows:
\p
\v 9 “King¦111746 Artahshashta to Ezra the¦111749 priest¦111750 and¦111751 reader of¦111753 the¦111753 master's law¦111754, greetings.
\v 10 Having determined to deal graciously, I've¦111760 given orders that¦111763 those of¦111766 the¦111766 nation¦111767 of the¦111768 Yehudim \add !(Jews)\add*, and¦111771 of the¦111772 priests¦111773 and¦111774 Levites, and¦111777 of those within our¦111781 realm who are willing and freely choose to, should go with you¦111784 to Yerushalem.
\v 11 As¦111787 many therefore¦111788 as are so disposed, let them depart with you, as it's seemed good both¦111794 to me and¦111795 my seven¦111797 friends¦111798 the counsellors,
\v 12 that¦111800 they may look to¦111803 the¦111804 affairs of Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* and¦111806 Yerushalem, in accordance¦111803 with what's in¦111811 the¦111812 master's law¦111813,
\v 13 and carry the gifts to the master of Yisrael to Yerushalem, which I and my friends have vowed, and that all the gold and silver that can be found in the country of Bavel for the master in Yerushalem,
\v 14 with that also which is given of the people for the temple of the master their god that's at Yerushalem, be collected: even the gold and silver for bulls, rams, and lambs, and what goes with them,
\v 15 to the end that they may offer sacrifices¦111883 to the¦111884 master on¦111886 the¦111887 altar¦111888 of¦111889 the¦111889 master their god¦111891, which is in¦111894 Yerushalem.
\v 16 Whatever you and your kindred decide to¦111905 do¦111905 with¦111901 gold¦111906 and¦111907 silver, do that according¦111910 to¦111910 your god's¦111914 will¦111912.
\v 17 The¦111917 holy vessels¦111919 of¦111920 the master, which are given you¦111924 for the¦111926 use of¦111928 your god's¦111931 temple¦111929, which is in Yerushalem,
\v 18 and whatever else you remember for the use of your god's temple, give¦111933 it out¦111934 of¦111935 the¦111935 king's treasury¦111937.
\v 19 I¦111938, King¦111941 Artahshashta \add !(Artaxerxes)\add*, have also commanded the keepers of the treasures in¦111948 Aram \add !(Syria)\add* and Foinikai, that¦111948 whatever Ezra the¦111953 priest¦111954 and¦111955 reader of¦111957 the¦111959 Most High God's¦111960 law¦111958 sends¦111951 for, they should give¦111964 it¦111965 to him with all diligence,
\v 20 to the sum of one hundred talents of silver, likewise also of wheat even to one hundred cors,\f + \fr 8:20 \ft a cor is about 230 litres, so 100 cors is about 23 kilolitres or 652 bushels\f* and one hundred firkins\f + \fr 8:20 \ft a firkin is about 41 litres or 11 gallons.\f* of wine, and\f + \fr 8:20 \ft So some authorities. See Ezra 7:22. The common reading is, \fqa other things.\f* salt in abundance.
\v 21 Let all things be performed after God's law diligently to the most high God, that anger come not onto the kingdom of the king and his sons.
\v 22 I command¦112014 you¦112012 also¦112013 that¦112015 no tax, nor any other imposition, be laid¦112044 on any of the¦112017 priests¦112018, or Levites, or holy singers, or gatekeepers, or temple servants, or any that have employment in this¦112020 temple, and that no man¦112034 has¦112042 authority¦112043 to impose any tax on them.
\v 23 You¦112048, Ezra, according¦112050 to¦112050 God's¦112054 wisdom¦112052, ordain judges and¦112057 justices that¦112059 they may judge¦112056 in¦112061 all¦112062 Aram and¦112064 Foinikai all¦112066 those who¦112067 know your god's¦112072 law¦112070; and¦112074 those who don't¦112076 know it, you must teach.
\v 24 Anyone who transgresses the¦112084 law¦112085 of¦112086 your god¦112087 and of the king will be punished diligently, whether it be by death¦112097, or other punishment¦112101, by penalty of money, or by imprisonment.”
\p
\v 25 Then¦112107 Ezra the¦112110 scribe¦112111 said¦112108, “Blessed be the only master, the¦112115 god¦112116 of my fathers¦112118, who's¦112120 put these things into¦112121 the¦112126 king's¦112127 heart¦112125, to¦112128 glorify¦112128 his house¦112130 that's¦112132 in¦112133 Yerushalem,
\v 26 and¦112135 has honoured me in¦112138 the sight of¦112138 the¦112139 king¦112140, his counsellors, and all¦112145 his friends¦112147 and¦112148 nobles.
\v 27 Therefore I¦112152 was¦112154 encouraged by the¦112156 help of¦112159 the¦112159 master my god¦112160, and¦112162 gathered together out¦112165 of¦112166 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* men¦112164 to go up with me.
\s1 The families travelling with Ezra
\p
\v 28 These are the¦112173 chief according¦112175 to¦112175 their families¦112177 and¦112179 their several divisions, who went up with¦112184 me from¦112186 Bavel \add !(Babylon)\add* in¦112188 King¦112193 Artahshashta's \add !(Artaxerxes)\add* reign:
\v 29 of the¦112195 sons¦112196 of Pinhas, Gereshom; of the¦112200 sons¦112201 of Itamar, Daniyel; of the¦112205 sons¦112206 of David,\f + \fr 8:29 \fqa Hattush.\f* Hatush\f + \fr 8:29 \ft Ezra 8:3, \fqa of the sons of Shecaniah; of the sons of Parosh.\f* the¦112209 son of Shekanyah;
\v 30 of the¦112212 sons¦112213 of Par'osh, Zekaryah \add !(Zechariah)\add*; and¦112216 with¦112217 him were counted one hundred¦112221 and fifty¦112222 men¦112220;
\v 31 of the sons of Pahat-Moav, Elyehoeynay the¦112224 son¦112225 of\f + \fr 8:31 \fqa Zerehiah.\f* Zerahyah, and¦112230 with¦112231 him two¦112234 hundred¦112234 men¦112233;
\v 32 of\f + \fr 8:32 \ft Ezra 8:5, \fqa of the sons of Shecaniah, the son of Jahaziel.\f* the sons of Zatu, Shekanyah the¦112236 son¦112237 of Yahaziel, and¦112241 with¦112242 him three¦112245 hundred¦112245 men; of the¦112247 sons¦112248 of Adin¦112249, Ovadyah \add !(Obadiah)\add* the son of Yonatan \add !(Jonathan)\add*, and¦112252 with¦112253 him two¦112256 hundred¦112256 and fifty¦112257 men;
\v 33 of the¦112259 sons of Eylam, Yeshaeyah son¦112260 of Atalyah \add !(Athaliah)\add*, and¦112264 with¦112265 him seventy¦112268 men¦112267;
\v 34 of the¦112270 sons of Shefatyah, Zevadyah son¦112271 of Mika'el \add !(Michael)\add*, and¦112275 with¦112276 him seventy¦112279 men¦112278;
\v 35 of the¦112281 sons of Yoav \add !(Joab)\add*, Ovadyah son¦112282 of Yehiel. Yehiel, and¦112286 with¦112287 him two¦112290 hundred¦112290 and twelve¦112291 men¦112289;
\v 36 of the¦112293 sons of Bani, Shelomit son¦112294 of Yosifyah,\f + \fr 8:36 \ft Ezra 8:10, \fqa of the sons of Shelomith, the son of Josiphiah.\f* and¦112298 with¦112299 him one hundred¦112304 and sixty¦112302 men¦112301;
\v 37 of the¦112306 sons of Bevay, Zekaryah son¦112307 of Bevay, and¦112311 with¦112312 him twenty-eight¦112315 men¦112314;
\v 38 of the¦112317 sons of Azgad: Azgad, Yohan \add !(John)\add* son¦112318 of Hakatan Hakatan, and¦112322 with¦112323 him one hundred¦112326 and ten¦112327 men¦112325;
\v 39 of the¦112329 sons¦112330 of Adonikam¦112331, the¦112332 last¦112333, and¦112334 these are the¦112336 names¦112337 of¦112340 them, Elifelet, Ye'uel, and¦112342 Shemayah, and¦112344 with¦112345 them seventy¦112348 men¦112347;
\v 40 of the¦112350 sons of Bigvay, Utay the son¦112351 of¦112355 Zabud, and¦112357 with¦112358 him seventy¦112361 men¦112360.
\s1 Ezra prepares the group for the journey
\p
\v 41 I gathered them together to the¦112366 river¦112369 called Ahava. There we pitched our tents three¦112373 days¦112372, and¦112375 I inspected them.
\v 42 When¦112378 I'd found¦112387 there¦112388 none of the¦112380 priests¦112381 and¦112382 Levites,
\v 43 then sent¦112389 I to¦112390 Eleazar, Ariel, Shemayah,
\v 44 Elnatan, Shemayah, Yoyariv, Natan \add !(Nathan)\add*, Elnatan, Zekaryah, and Meshulam, principal men and men of understanding.
\v 45 I asked¦112414 them to¦112416 go¦112416 to¦112417 Ido the¦112419 captain, who was in¦112422 the¦112423 place¦112424 of¦112425 the¦112425 treasury¦112426,
\v 46 and¦112431 commanded them that¦112432 they should speak to Ido, to his kindred, and¦112435 to the¦112436 treasurers in¦112437 that¦112438 place¦112439, to¦112441 send¦112441 us such men as might execute the priests’ office in our master's house¦112447.
\v 47 By the¦112455 mighty¦112456 hand¦112457 of¦112458 our master, they brought¦112452 to¦112454 us men¦112461 of understanding of the¦112463 sons¦112464 of¦112466\f + \fr 8:47 \fqa Mahli.\f* Mahli the¦112466 son of¦112468 Levi, the¦112468 son of Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*,\f + \fr 8:47 \fqa Sherebiah.\f* Shereveyah, and¦112471 his sons¦112473, and¦112475 his kindred, who¦112476 were¦112478 eighteen,
\v 48 and\f + \fr 8:48 \fqa Hashabiah.\f* Hashavyah, Annuus, and Osaias his brother¦112488, of the¦112490 sons¦112491 of Chanuneus, and¦112493 their sons¦112495 were twenty¦112497 men¦112498;
\v 49 and¦112499 of the¦112501 temple servants whom David and¦112506 the¦112507 principal men had appointed for the¦112510 servants of the¦112512 Levites, two¦112515 hundred¦112515 and¦112516 twenty¦112517 temple servants. The¦112520 list of¦112521 all¦112518 their names¦112521 was reported.
\s1 Prayer and preparations for a safe journey
\p
\v 50 There¦112524 I vowed a fast¦112525 for the¦112526 young men before¦112528 our master, to¦112531 seek¦112531 from¦112532 him a prosperous journey both¦112536 for us and¦112537 for our children¦112541 and¦112543 livestock that were with us;
\v 51 for¦112546 I was ashamed to¦112547 ask¦112547 of the¦112548 king¦112549 infantry, cavalry, and an escort for¦112556 protection against our adversaries.
\v 52 Because¦112564 we'd said to the¦112565 king¦112566 that¦112567 our master's power¦112569 would be¦112573 with¦112574 those who¦112575 seek him, to support them in all¦112579 ways.
\v 53 Again¦112582 we prayed to our lord¦112585 about¦112584 these things, and¦112589 found him to be merciful.
\p
\v 54 Then¦112592 I set apart twelve men of the¦112594 chiefs of the¦112596 priests¦112597,\f + \fr 8:54 \fqa Sherebiah, Hashabiah.\f* Shereveyah, Hashavyah, and ten men of their kindred with¦112605 them.
\v 55 I weighed out to them the¦112616 silver, the¦112619 gold¦112620, and¦112621 the¦112622 holy vessels¦112624 of¦112625 our master's house¦112626, which¦112630 the¦112632 king¦112633, his counsellors, the nobles, and all¦112642 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add* had given¦112631.
\v 56 When¦112644 I'd weighed it, I delivered¦112646 to¦112646 them six¦112650 hundred¦112650 and fifty¦112651 talents of silver, silver vessels weighing one hundred talents, one hundred talents of gold,
\v 57 twenty¦112663 golden vessels, and¦112664 twelve¦112673 vessels of brass, even of fine brass, glittering like gold.
\v 58 I said¦112675 to¦112675 them, “You're¦112678 holy¦112679 to¦112680 the¦112681 master, the¦112684 vessels¦112685 are holy¦112687, and¦112688 the¦112689 gold¦112690 and¦112691 the¦112692 silver are a¦112694 vow¦112694 to the¦112695 master, the¦112698 master of our fathers¦112699.
\v 59 Watch¦112701 and¦112702 keep them until¦112704 you deliver¦112706 them to the¦112709 chiefs of the¦112711 priests¦112712 and¦112713 Levites, and¦112716 to¦112718 the¦112719 principal men of¦112721 the¦112721 families of Yisrael in¦112723 Yerushalem, in¦112725 the¦112726 chambers of¦112728 our master's house¦112729.
\v 60 So¦112733 the priests¦112737 and¦112738 the Levites who received the silver, the¦112744 gold¦112745, and¦112746 the¦112747 vessels¦112748 which were in¦112750 Yerushalem, brought them into the¦112756 master's temple¦112755.
\s1 The group arrives in Yerushalem
\p
\v 61 We left the¦112761 river¦112762 Ahava on the¦112764 twelfth day of¦112766 the¦112766 first¦112767 month. We came to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* by the¦112774 mighty¦112775 hand¦112776 of¦112777 our master which was on us. The master delivered¦112784 us from every¦112790 enemy¦112791 on the way, and¦112792 so we came to¦112793 Yerushalem.
\v 62 When¦112796 we'd been¦112797 there three days, the silver and¦112808 gold¦112810 was weighed and delivered¦112811 in¦112812 our master's house¦112814 on the¦112803 fourth¦112804 day to\f + \fr 8:62 \fqa Meremoth.\f* Meremot the priest¦112819 the son of\f + \fr 8:62 \fqa Uriah.\f* Uriyah.
\v 63 With¦112821 him was Eleazar¦112823 the¦112824 son of¦112825 Pinhas, and¦112827 with¦112829 them were Yozavad the son of Yeshua \add !(Jesus)\add* and\f + \fr 8:63 \fqa Noadiah the son of Binnui.\f* Noadyah the son of Binuy, the Levites. All was delivered to¦112839 them by number¦112840 and weight.
\v 64 All the¦112847 weight of them was recorded at the¦112851 same hour¦112852.
\v 65 Moreover those who'd¦112853 come¦112855 out¦112856 of captivity offered sacrifices to the master, the¦112861 god¦112862 of¦112863 Yisrael, even twelve¦112867 bulls¦112866 for¦112868 all¦112869 Yisrael, ninety-six rams,
\v 66 seventy-two¦112874 lambs¦112873, and twelve goats for a peace offering—all¦112879 of them a sacrifice¦112880 to the¦112881 master.
\v 67 They delivered the king's commandments to the king's stewards and¦112892 to the¦112893 governors of Coele-Syria and¦112897 Foinikai; and¦112899 they honoured the¦112901 people and¦112903 the¦112906 master's temple¦112905.
\s1 Ezra learns about marriages to foreigners
\p
\v 68 Now when these things were done, the¦112913 principal men came to me and¦112908 said,
\v 69 “The¦112918 nation¦112919 of¦112920 Yisrael, the princes, the priests¦112927, and¦112928 the¦112929 Levites haven't put away¦112940 from¦112940 themselves the¦112931 foreign people of the¦112934 land¦112935 nor the¦112937 uncleannesses of the¦112941 Gentiles—the¦112943 Kena'anim \add !(Canaanites)\add*, Hitim, Perizi, Yevusim, Moavim, Mitsrim \add !(Egyptians)\add*, and Edomim.
\v 70 Because¦112958 both they and their sons¦112967 have married with their daughters¦112961, and the¦112973 holy¦112974 seed¦112972 is mixed with the¦112976 foreign people of the¦112979 land¦112980. From¦112991 the¦112992 beginning¦112993 of¦112994 this matter the rulers and the nobles have been partakers of this iniquity.”
\s1 Ezra confesses the people's sins
\p
\v 71 And¦112996 as soon as I'd heard¦112999 these things, I¦113000 tore my clothes¦113004 and¦113005 my holy garment, and¦113009 plucked the hair from off my head¦113014 and¦113015 beard, and¦113018 sat down sad and¦113021 full of heaviness.
\v 72 So¦113023 all those who were moved at the word of the master, the god¦113034 of¦113035 Yisrael, assembled to me while I mourned for the¦113040 iniquity, but¦113042 I sat still full of heaviness until¦113045 the¦113046 evening sacrifice¦113048.
\v 73 Then¦113049 rising up from¦113051 the fast with my clothes¦113057 and my holy garment torn, and bowing my knees¦113064 and¦113065 stretching¦113066 out¦113066 my hands¦113068 to¦113069 the¦113070 master,
\v 74 I said, “Oh master, I'm ashamed and¦113075 confounded before your face¦113078,
\v 75 for¦113081 our sins¦113082 are multiplied above¦113085 our heads¦113087, and¦113089 our errors have reached up to heaven¦113096
\v 76 ever since the¦113099 time¦113100 of our fathers¦113102. We're¦113105 in¦113106 great¦113107 sin¦113108, even to this¦113110 day¦113111.
\v 77 Because¦113114 our sins¦113116 and¦113118 our fathers¦113120’ we with our kindred, our kings¦113130, and¦113132 our priests¦113135 were given up to the¦113137 kings¦113138 of the¦113139 earth¦113140, to the sword¦113142, and¦113143 to captivity¦113144, and¦113145 for a prey with¦113147 shame¦113148, to this¦113150 day¦113152.
\v 78 Now¦113154 in some measure mercy¦113160 has been shown to us from¦113161 you, Oh master, that there should be left¦113165 us a root¦113167 and¦113168 a name¦113169 in¦113170 the¦113171 place¦113172 of your sanctuary,
\v 79 and¦113175 to uncover a light in¦113180 the¦113181 house¦113182 of¦113184 the¦113184 master our god¦113185, and to¦113187 give¦113187 us food¦113189 in¦113190 the¦113191 time¦113192 of our servitude.
\v 80 Yes, when¦113196 we were in¦113197 bondage, we¦113200 weren't forsaken by¦113203 our master, but¦113207 he gave us favour before¦113212 Paras' \add !(Persia)\add* kings¦113214, so that they gave us food,
\v 81 glorified¦113220 our master's temple¦113222, and¦113226 raised up the¦113228 desolate Tsiyon \add !(Zion)\add*, to¦113231 give¦113231 us a sure dwelling in¦113234 Yehudah \add !(Judea)\add* and¦113237 Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*.
\p
\v 82 “Now, Oh master, what can we say, having these things? Because we've transgressed your commandments which you gave by the hand of your servants the prophets, saying,
\v 83 ‘The land, which you enter into to possess as an inheritance, is a land polluted with the pollutions of the foreigners of the land, and they've filled it with their uncleanness.
\v 84 Therefore now¦113283 you¦113286 mustn't¦113287 marry your daughters¦113294 to¦113297 their sons, and you mustn't take¦113297 their daughters for your sons¦113299.
\v 85 You must never seek¦113303 to have peace with them, that¦113311 you may be strong, and eat¦113313 the¦113314 good things of the¦113316 land¦113317, and¦113318 that¦113320 you¦113322 may leave it for an¦113324 inheritance to your children¦113321 forever.’
\v 86 All¦113328 that's happened is¦113330 done to¦113330 us for¦113331 our wicked¦113336 works¦113333 and¦113337 great¦113339 sins, for you, Oh master, made our sins light,
\v 87 and gave¦113350 to¦113350 us such¦113352 a root¦113353; but we've turned back again¦113354 to transgress your law¦113358 in mingling ourselves with the uncleanness of the heathen of the land¦113368.
\v 88 You weren't angry with us to¦113372 destroy¦113372 us until¦113374 you'd left us neither root¦113378, seed¦113380, nor name¦113382.
\v 89 Oh master of¦113385 Yisrael \add !(Israel)\add*, you're true¦113387, for¦113390 we're left a root¦113391 this¦113393 day.
\v 90 Listen, now¦113396 we're¦113397 before¦113398 you¦113399 in¦113400 our iniquities, for¦113405 we can't stand¦113407 any longer before¦113409 you¦113410 because of these things.”
\s1 The people agree to act
\p
\v 91 As Ezra in his prayer¦113415 made his confession, weeping¦113418, and lying flat on the ground before¦113420 the¦113421 temple¦113422, a very¦113430 great throng of men¦113431, women¦113433, and¦113434 children gathered to him from Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add*; for¦113437 there was¦113438 great¦113439 weeping among¦113440 the¦113441 multitude¦113442.\x + \xo 8:91: \xt Ezr 10:1.\x*
